# Add a repository

A repository implements domain ports on the request's `AsyncSession`, maps rows to domain
objects and back, and turns database errors into domain errors. Tables change only through
reviewed migrations. The rules are in
[persistence.md](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md).

## Steps

1. **Port first.** The reads and writes the use case needs, as Protocols in
   `domain/<feature>/ports.py` (`RecipeReader`, `RecipeWriter`), with the domain errors
   they raise ([models.md](../../../docs/conventions/models.md#domain-models)).
2. **Table.** A class in `infrastructure/db/models.py` subclassing `Base`, typed with
   `Mapped[...]` and `mapped_column()`; no hand-written constraint names; relationships
   `lazy="raise"` ([models](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#models)).
3. **Migration.** `make migrate`, then `make migration name="<what changed>"`; both use
   the PostgreSQL at `DB__URL` in `.env` (locally the one in meal-platform compose). Review
   the file: renames, server defaults and data are not autogenerated; write `downgrade()`;
   remove the "auto generated" comments
   ([writing a migration](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#writing-a-migration)).
   It must work with the release still running
   ([expand, then contract](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#expand-then-contract)).
4. **Repository** in `infrastructure/db/<feature>.py`: `__init__` takes the `AsyncSession`;
   queries with `select()` or `session.get()`; `add()` flushes so a duplicate key becomes
   the feature's `ConflictError` subclass there; it never commits
   ([repositories](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#repositories),
   [queries](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#queries)).
5. **Wire it.** The use case's provider in `api/dependencies.py` takes
   `session: DbSessionDep` and builds the repository: one transaction per request.
6. **Tests**, marked `integration`: the repository with `db_session` /
   `db_session_factory` (found, missing, conflict, mapping both ways); routes with
   `db_client` and `get_app_state` overridden
   ([integration tests](../../../docs/conventions/testing.md#integration-tests)). Use cases
   keep using fakes of the ports.
7. `make check` (needs Docker). `test_models_match_migrations` fails when a model change has
   no migration.

## Worked example

[A recipes table](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#example-a-recipes-table) goes
through every step: `RecipeReader` / `RecipeWriter` (step 1, in models.md), `RecipeRow`
(2), the migration as `make migration` wrote it (3), `SqlRecipeRepository` (4),
`get_add_recipe` (5), and `tests/infrastructure/db/test_recipes.py` with
`tests/api/test_recipes.py` (6). A long-running index comes later in its own revision
([long-running operations](../../../docs/conventions/persistence.md#long-running-operations)).
